					<description><![CDATA[<p>Multiplier Raises $35 Million To Accelerate AI Growth Multiplier has raised $35 million in Series B funding to expand its AI-powered professional services platform. The round was led by The</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://ventureburn.com/multiplier-raises-35-million-series-b/" data-wpel-link="internal">Multiplier Raises $35 Million To Expand AI-Powered Professional Services Platform</a> appeared first on <a href="https://ventureburn.com" data-wpel-link="internal">Ventureburn</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<h2><b>Multiplier Raises $35 Million To Accelerate AI Growth</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Multiplier has raised $35 million in Series B funding to expand its AI-powered professional services platform. The round was led by The General Partnership. Existing investors Ribbit Capital and Lightspeed Venture Partners also participated.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The funding will support additional acquisitions of specialist professional services firms. It will also help the company grow its technology and operations teams as demand for AI-enabled business services increases.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Multiplier operates a permanent holding company model.The company purchases existing companies but lets them keep their names, management, and much of their autonomy. Rather than substituting AI for people it is instead building AI-powered products that boost their efficiency and service to clients.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">AI should be used to empower working professionals, not replace them, Founder and CEO Noah Pepper argued in a company blog post outlining the technology. He believes AI tools enable them to allocate their time to “judgment based work,” while weeding out menial tasks.</span></p>
<h2><b>Company Expands AI Capabilities Across Professional Firms</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Multiplier embeds its engineering teams directly within acquired firms. It has also employed more than 30 technologists, whose work with subject matter experts leads to AI tools designed around the needs of a specific business. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Since the businesses that use their technology are not solely owned by third party software companies, multiplier employees have access to customer and supplier databases and, in the words of its founders, &#8220;access to customers, products and processes. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The company&#8217;s model targets industries where expert capacity limits growth. Many professional services firms rely heavily on experienced practitioners and manage information across disconnected systems. Multiplier believes AI can automate preparation and routine tasks while leaving final decisions to qualified professionals.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The company has completed eight acquisitions since launch. Five of those deals closed during the past year. It also has four additional firms under signed term sheets. Together, its network now serves clients in more than 10 countries.</span></p>
<h2><b>Funding Supports Expansion And Leadership Growth<br />
</b></h2>
<div id="attachment_204016" style="width: 1322px" class="wp-caption alignnone"><img decoding="async" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-204016" class="size-full wp-image-204016" src="https://ventureburn.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/a-futuristic-poster-showcases-a-vibrant-_vAYGCKGTWqeCE7wZ1IRkdA_terKSRWEQTagMXjH0CHxTw.png" alt="A neon futuristic visual showing AI-powered tools supporting professionals across business operations." width="1312" height="736" /><p id="caption-attachment-204016" class="wp-caption-text">Multiplier scales AI-driven operations to enhance professional services efficiency and growth. Source: Created by Ventureburn</p></div>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The latest investment also coincides with a major executive appointment.  At Multiplier, he will oversee finance, operations, partnerships, people and the company&#8217;s expanding San Francisco office. The company believes this approach scales more effectively while preserving valuable client relationships and professional expertise over time.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Allen Shim, former Slack CFO, now serves as President and Chief Financial Officer at Multiplier successfully. The company will use the funding to build scalable technology, people, and operational process architecture efficiently.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Multiplier aims supporting long-term growth while preserving each acquired business&#8217;s autonomy and specialised professional </span><a href="https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/expertise" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener sponsored external noreferrer" data-wpel-link="external"><span style="font-weight: 400">expertise</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400"> independently. Shim previously guided Slack through its successful initial public offering before the company&#8217;s Salesforce acquisition successfully completed.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">According to The General Partnership, accounting and other professional services markets continue to face capacity challenges despite growing demand. The investment firm believes Multiplier&#8217;s approach enables trusted professionals to serve more clients without reducing service quality.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">More News: </span><a href="https://ventureburn.com/horizon3-raises-250-million/" data-wpel-link="internal"><span style="font-weight: 400">Horizon3 Raises $250 Million to Expand AI-Powered Cybersecurity Platform</span></a></p>
<h2><b>Multiplier Focuses On Long-Term Industry Transformation</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The new capital will primarily fund additional acquisitions and continued development of proprietary AI solutions. Multiplier is set to grow its specialist firms and to enhance its technological capabilities. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Multiplier&#8217;s investment approach differs from traditional buy-and-build strategies that fully replace company founders after acquisitions. Instead, founders remain in senior leadership positions while receiving long-term capital and operational management expertise continuously.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">To stay updated on crypto venture capital funding and market trends, visit our </span><a href="https://ventureburn.com/category/news/venture-capital/" data-wpel-link="internal"><span style="font-weight: 400">venture capital news section</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400"> for more insights.</span></p>
