		<category><![CDATA[Series A]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://ventureburn.com/?p=203960</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>Europe has a renewable problem that isn’t expensive to solve. The concern with wind and solar, while cheap, is that they disappear. Ore Energy raises $43 million in series A</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://ventureburn.com/ore-energy-raises-43-million-series-a-for-iron-air-batteries/" data-wpel-link="internal">Ore Energy Raises $43 Million to Build Lasting Rust Batteries for the AI Era</a> appeared first on <a href="https://ventureburn.com" data-wpel-link="internal">Ventureburn</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Europe has a renewable problem that isn’t expensive to solve. The concern with wind and solar, while cheap, is that they disappear. Ore Energy </span><a href="https://lnkd.in/p/eiGqS4Fe" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener external noreferrer" data-wpel-link="external"><span style="font-weight: 400">raises $43 million</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400"> in series A to solve that problem. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The money will be used to expand production of iron-air batteries that can store power for up to 100 hours at about one-tenth the cost of lithium-ion. Ore is saying you don’t need gas if you can store electricity for days. AI is breaking the grid. Electricity used in global data centers is set to increase to 945 TWh by 2030. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">AI workloads make demand spike in ways utilities are not prepared to handle. Likewise, Europe cannot account for an estimated 72 TWh of wind and solar each year because there’s nowhere to put it when it’s windy and sunny. That wasted power is worth about $8 billion. </span></p>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400">Ore Energy Unveils Rust Batteries</span></h2>
<div id="attachment_203963" style="width: 1034px" class="wp-caption aligncenter"><img decoding="async" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-203963" class="size-large wp-image-203963" src="https://ventureburn.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Ore-Energy-Rust-Battery-1024x768.jpeg" alt="A white utility container prominently featuring the blue and black &quot;ORE ENERGY&quot; logo sits on a green lawn outdoors in front of a grid." width="1024" height="768" /><p id="caption-attachment-203963" class="wp-caption-text">Ore Energy Rust Battery</p></div>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Today, most grid batteries last between 4 and 12 hours. What Ore is building lasts for 100 hours. The makeup is simple. The battery uses electrodes, water, and air. To charge, it runs electricity backward to turn rust back into iron. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">To discharge, it lets the iron rust again and catches the energy. This explains why it is also called a breathing battery. It doesn’t use lithium and cobalt, so it’s affordable and can be built in Europe. Minerals do not need to be imported, nor supply chains activated. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The main component is iron which can be found everywhere. According to the startup’s CEO, the real competitor isn’t other batteries. It’s natural gas. On today’s grids, gas plants fire up and fill the gap when there’s a multi-day lull in wind or sun. The company wants to replace that with stored renewables.</span></p>
<p><b><i>More Updates: </i></b><a href="https://ventureburn.com/june-ai-raises-20-million-in-pre-seed-funding-to-automate-enterprise-ai-deployment/" data-wpel-link="internal"><b><i>June AI Raises $20M To Automate Enterprise AI Deployment</i></b></a></p>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400">How Ore Energy Operates</span></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Ore has about 50 people in Amsterdam. The company has signed a 1 gigawatt-hour agreement with Budget Thuis, a Dutch energy supplier. They’re also running pilots with French utility EDF.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The goal is to hit gigawatt-hour-scale production by 2028 and to make iron-air a core part of European grid infrastructure by 2035. For utilities, payments to curtail wind farms or firing up gas turbines will be replaced with buying cheap power when it is abundant and storing it for days. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">When it is needed, it will then be dispatched. For AI data centers, you can use renewables without outages with multi-day storage. </span></p>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400">The Funding Round and Energy Landscape</span></h2>
<div id="attachment_203962" style="width: 1034px" class="wp-caption aligncenter"><img decoding="async" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-203962" class="size-large wp-image-203962" src="https://ventureburn.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Ore-Energy-1024x537.jpg" alt="Three professionals stand side-by-side with arms folded against a light wooden slat wall featuring the large black letters of the &quot;ORE&quot; logo." width="1024" height="537" /><p id="caption-attachment-203962" class="wp-caption-text">Ore Energy Team</p></div>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The Ore Energy $43 million series A funding round was led by Plural and HV, with existing backer Positron Ventures joining in. It brings the total funding of Ore Energy to $61 million. It’s a modest round compared to other category leaders. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">US-based Form Energy has raised over $1.2B and is valued at $3.4B. They’re building a factory in West Virginia to make iron-air batteries at 500 MW per year by 2028. Companies like iwell and Terralayr are working on grid storage in Europe, too. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Rather than using iron-air, they’re focusing on shorter durations. Large rounds are becoming popular. While Ore’s funding is modest, it necessarily buys them time to scale.</span></p>
<p><b><i>More Updates: </i></b><a href="https://ventureburn.com/base-power-1b-series-d-base-core-battery/" data-wpel-link="internal"><b><i>Base Power Raises $1B To Mass Produce Batteries for Homes</i></b></a></p>
<p>The post <a href="https://ventureburn.com/ore-energy-raises-43-million-series-a-for-iron-air-batteries/" data-wpel-link="internal">Ore Energy Raises $43 Million to Build Lasting Rust Batteries for the AI Era</a> appeared first on <a href="https://ventureburn.com" data-wpel-link="internal">Ventureburn</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
			</item>
