										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<h2><b>Zenity Raises $125 Million To Accelerate AI Agent Security</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">AI security platform Zenity raised $125 million in a Series C funding round for enterprise expansion. The Boston and Tel Aviv-based company secures artificial intelligence agents operating across large enterprise organisations worldwide today.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Norwest led the investment alongside Qumra Capital, SoftBank Vision Fund 2, and multiple strategic venture investors. Additional investors included Hitachi Ventures, LG Technology Ventures, Vertex Ventures, Third Point Ventures, DTCP, and Intel Capital.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The latest funding brings Zenity&#8217;s total capital raised to approximately $185 million since its founding successfully. The investment reflects strong market demand for securing expanding artificial intelligence agents across complex enterprise environments today.</span></p>
<h2><b>Funding Supports Platform Expansion And Global Growth</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The expansion and growth in the new, larger offices at One Embarcadero will enable Zenity to strengthen and scale up both its AI security platform and Zenity Labs as well as deepen its market impact in EMEA, as well as Europe and APAC. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Zenity plans to expand its global presence by growing international commercial operations across key strategic markets. The company will continue driving worldwide security standards for all enterprise artificial intelligence deployments across industries globally.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Zenity was founded in 2021 by serial security entrepreneurs Ben Kliger and Michael Bargury to build software for managing the security of AI agents. Over 230 professionals are already part of Zenity worldwide, with ongoing development work taking place in Tel Aviv and core commercial activity overseen from its New York office. </span></p>
<h2><b>Enterprise Demand Drives AI Security Adoption<br />
</b></h2>
<div id="attachment_203944" style="width: 1322px" class="wp-caption alignnone"><img decoding="async" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-203944" class="size-full wp-image-203944" src="https://ventureburn.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/a-futuristic-poster-rendered-in-a-vibran_y0BXdXveXSavh72onYYKSQ_6aQRqmM7SEyZ_9tnWtb4gA_cover.png" alt="A neon futuristic visual showing AI agents monitored by real-time security systems across enterprise platforms." width="1312" height="736" /><p id="caption-attachment-203944" class="wp-caption-text">Zenity enables secure, real-time governance of AI agents across complex enterprise environments. Source: Created by Ventureburn</p></div>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The surging enterprise AI race led to increased demand for the tech required to regulate autonomous agents deployed in sensitive domains. The customer pool at Zenity contains organizations within Fortune 500s and global 2000s industries such as fintech, biotech, Pharma, energy, and industrial.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Zenity nearly tripled its revenue for two consecutive years already this year and hopes to see it climb again as the pace to deploy AI in companies speeds up even further. Zenity analyzes its customer AI’s intent, “prior to its execution to approve, reject, or edit real-time.”</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Zenity supports AI agents built on major enterprise platforms, including Microsoft Copilot, ChatGPT Enterprise, Google Gemini, Microsoft Foundry, Google Vertex AI, Claude, Codex, and Cursor. This broad compatibility enables organisations to apply consistent governance across multiple AI environments.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">More News: </span><a href="https://ventureburn.com/siengine-secures-us-200-million/" data-wpel-link="internal"><span style="font-weight: 400">SiEngine Secures US$200 Million to Expand Automotive Chip Development and Global Growth</span></a></p>
<h2><b>Research Strengthens AI Agent Security Leadership</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Beyond its commercial platform, Zenity has established a strong reputation through cybersecurity research. Its Zenity Labs team has identified several high-profile vulnerabilities affecting enterprise AI systems and contributed to industry security frameworks such as OWASP Top 10 guidance and MITRE ATLAS.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The research team recently disclosed AgentFlayer, a new class of zero-click attacks capable of compromising enterprise AI agents without user interaction. It has also uncovered vulnerabilities affecting Microsoft Copilot Studio, Perplexity&#8217;s Comet browser, and connected enterprise services that could expose sensitive organisational data.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Industry recognition has further strengthened Zenity&#8217;s position. Earlier this year, Gartner identified the company as a leading vendor in AI agent governance, highlighting its purpose-built architecture and intent-aware security capabilities.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">As organisations increasingly rely on AI agents to automate critical operations, Zenity expects demand for specialised governance platforms to continue growing. The latest funding provides additional resources to expand globally while advancing security technologies that help enterprises deploy AI agents safely and at scale.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">To stay updated on crypto venture capital funding and market trends, visit our </span><a href="https://ventureburn.com/category/news/venture-capital/" data-wpel-link="internal"><span style="font-weight: 400">venture capital news section</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400"> for more insights.</span></p>
